---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { url } from '@/lib/url';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="How WhatisAI stores your progress and uses your account information.">
  <article class="container section account-page prose">
    <div class="eyebrow">Your learning stays yours</div><h1>Privacy at WhatisAI</h1>
    <h2>Learn without an account</h2><p>Reading lessons does not require sign-in. Progress, quiz results, review schedules, and your theme choice are stored in your browser. Clearing browser storage removes those local records. Use the export control on <a href={url('/progress/')}>Your progress</a> to keep a copy.</p>
    <h2>When you sign in</h2><p>Google and Firebase Authentication handle sign-in. WhatisAI uses your account identifier, display name, and email address to identify your account. We do not receive your Google password or request access to Gmail, Drive, or contacts. Firebase may process technical information needed to run authentication and prevent abuse.</p>
    <h2>Your progress and cloud saves</h2><p>Signed-in progress is stored separately from guest progress on this device. Choosing “Save to account” uploads your learning progress to Google Cloud Firestore. It includes module status, quiz scores, confidence ratings, review schedules, placement results, and learning activity dates. Saves are private to your account under the database access rules; the service operator and infrastructure providers can administer the service. Cloud saves are manual, not continuous sync.</p>
    <h2>Sharing</h2><p>Share buttons send only the public page link and title. Your account details, scores, and private progress are not included. Anyone with a lesson link can read it without logging in.</p>
    <h2>Optional visitor analytics</h2><p>If you choose “Allow analytics,” PostHog receives page visits, referral domains, device and browser information, reading depth, link destinations, and learning activity events such as starting or finishing a challenge. A random browser identifier stored on this device helps count returning visitors. We do not connect it to your Google account or send your name, email, quiz answers, scores, confidence ratings, goal dates, or progress records. URL query strings and fragments are removed. Session recordings, automatic form capture, advertising, and person profiles are disabled.</p>
    <p>Analytics starts only after your permission. Declining or withdrawing permission stops collection; browser Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control signals also disable it. Use “Analytics preferences” at the bottom of any page to change your choice. Withdrawal clears the analytics identifier on this device and stops future collection; it does not delete events already received by PostHog. The free PostHog plan provides one year of event retention. See <a href="https://posthog.com/privacy">PostHog’s privacy policy</a>.</p>
    <h2>Lesson videos and external learning</h2><p>Embedded videos connect to YouTube’s privacy-enhanced player only after you choose “Load video here.” Playback is governed by the provider’s policies. Direct source links and reading alternatives work without loading the embedded player. External courses manage their own accounts, progress, and badges.</p>
    <h2>Third-party services</h2><p>The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. Account features use Google Firebase. Pages may load credited images from publishers or link to external research; those providers receive normal web requests. Optional analytics uses PostHog as described above; WhatisAI does not add advertising trackers. Provider processing is governed by their own privacy information, including <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google</a> and <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub</a>.</p>
    <h2>Export and deletion</h2><p>Export or reset local progress from Your progress. Delete your cloud save or your account from <a href={url('/account/')}>Your account</a>. Cloud saves remain until replaced or deleted. Signing out clears the account progress cached in this browser. Guest data, downloaded exports, and cached data on other devices must be removed separately.</p>
    <h2>Questions</h2><p>For account or service questions, email <a href="mailto:whatisai-support@googlegroups.com">whatisai-support@googlegroups.com</a>. Do not send passwords or authentication codes.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
